cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OTShield Bench, please cite the software release."
title: "OTShield Bench"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Jayachandra Reddy"
    family-names: "Palle"
version: "0.6.0-alpha"
date-released: 2026-09-22
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ASHTHRA/otshield-bench"
url: "https://github.com/ASHTHRA/otshield-bench"
abstract: >-
  OTShield Bench is a reproducible, vendor-neutral benchmark for operational
  technology cyber-detection effectiveness, resource cost, and resilience under
  degraded connectivity. Version 0.6.0-alpha is a research release candidate
  with 125 completed isolated OpenPLC condition runs across five network
  conditions, pairing a fixed baseline detector with an independently calibrated
  robust detector on identical read-only Modbus/TCP Function Code 3 captures.
  The robust threshold showed greater resilience under the heavier tested delay
  conditions with no observed recall/F1 penalty under clean and lighter tested
  conditions. Results are limited to the documented laboratory and timing setup;
  they do not establish production validation, universal superiority, full GRFICS
  validation, DNP3 or EtherNet/IP validation, external replication, or adoption.
keywords:
  - operational technology
  - industrial control systems
  - cybersecurity
  - Modbus TCP
  - OpenPLC
  - detection benchmarking
  - resilience
  - reproducibility
